title: ShieldBreak Defender LPE conhost.exe Spawned by wer.dll
id: c497a56c-4ef8-48b3-b3e0-00e2a6892b4b
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects the terminal process-creation step of the ShieldBreak
    local privilege escalation chain (Nightmare Eclipse, Aug 2026),
    which abuses Microsoft Defender's cloud-hydration scan: a hydrated
    phoneinfo.dll is loaded by wer.dll (Windows Error Reporting), which
    then spawns conhost.exe running as SYSTEM on fully patched
    Windows 11 25H2 and Windows Server 2025. This is a patch bypass
    for CVE-2026-50656 (RoguePlanet) in mpengine.dll.
references:
    - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/new-microsoft-defender-shieldbreak-zero-day-grants-system-privileges/
    - https://cyberpress.org/shieldbreak-windows-defender-zero-day-bypasses/
    - https://gbhackers.com/shieldbreak-windows-defender-0-day/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/08/13
tags:
    - attack.t1068
    - attack.t1574
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_parent:
        ParentImage|endswith: '\wer.dll'
    selection_child:
        Image|endswith: '\conhost.exe'
        IntegrityLevel: 'System'
    condition: selection_parent and selection_child
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate Windows Error Reporting flows where wer.dll-hosted WER infrastructure spawns conhost.exe as SYSTEM; corroborate with cfapi cloud-sync-provider registration and QueueReporting scheduled task creation
level: high
---
title: ShieldBreak Defender LPE QueueReporting Scheduled Task
id: 16f76ba4-1931-4840-8915-3c8d4870e033
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects creation of the QueueReporting scheduled task used by the
    ShieldBreak Microsoft Defender local privilege escalation exploit
    (Nightmare Eclipse, Aug 2026; patch bypass for CVE-2026-50656 /
    RoguePlanet). The exploit registers a temporary directory as a Cloud
    Sync provider, plants an EICAR file, steers a Defender cloud-hydration
    scan at System32, and abuses CLFS-based identity file swapping; the
    QueueReporting scheduled task is one of the observable artifacts
    documented for the chain.
references:
    - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/new-microsoft-defender-shieldbreak-zero-day-grants-system-privileges/
    - https://www.securityweek.com/nightmare-eclipse-drops-windows-zero-day-exploit-shieldbreak/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/08/13
tags:
    - attack.t1068
    - attack.t1053
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_schtasks:
        Image|endswith: '\schtasks.exe'
        CommandLine|contains: 'QueueReporting'
    selection_powershell:
        Image|endswith:
            - '\powershell.exe'
            - '\pwsh.exe'
        CommandLine|contains|all:
            - 'Register-ScheduledTask'
            - 'QueueReporting'
    condition: selection_schtasks or selection_powershell
falsepositives:
    - Internal tooling that reuses the QueueReporting task name; verify against Defender cloud-sync registration and wer.dll process trees
level: high
